usage: project_classification.py [-h] [--organization ORGANIZATION]
                                 [--repository REPOSITORY] [--project PROJECT]
                                 [--limit LIMIT] [--apply] [--no-add-missing]
                                 [--skip-without-token]

Conservatively classify and synchronise existing GitHub Projects V2 items.
Work Type, Subsystem and Priority come only from unambiguous conventional
title prefixes and explicit labels; existing values are never overwritten.
Status is derived from GitHub facts (issue/PR state, draft flag and an
explicit ``blocked`` label). Terminal facts win: a merged PR or an issue
closed as completed becomes Done. Manually chosen statuses outside the managed
set are left untouched. Project Status is organisational only; it never
replaces a GitHub Actions result. Open issues and pull requests of the
repository that are missing from the project are added (bounded per run).
Nothing is added when the project scan was truncated, so the dry-run and apply
outputs stay exact. No issue, PR, label or milestone is modified.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --organization ORGANIZATION
  --repository REPOSITORY
  --project PROJECT
  --limit LIMIT
  --apply
  --no-add-missing      Do not add open issues/PRs missing from the project
  --skip-without-token  Exit 0 with a warning when the token is not configured
